<h2>How can I compare readings in a practical way?</h2>
<p><strong>Write down the source and time, then note what was going on.</strong> Try not to name a cause for every change.</p>
<p>Our <a href="/resources/stress-sleep-journal/">free stress and sleep journal</a> gives you a place to record routines and observations. A pattern in the journal is a question to look into, not proof of cause and effect.</p>

